WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.307
NumPy can sort values and also tell us where the minimum or maximum occurs.

00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:09.992
In this example, we have revenue values from five observations.

00:00:09.992 --> 00:00:14.037
N P dot sort returns the values in ascending order.

00:00:14.037 --> 00:00:22.252
The max method returns the largest revenue value, while argmax returns the position where that largest value

00:00:22.252 --> 00:00:26.677
occurs. The same pattern applies to the minimum using min and argmin.

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:30.232
Click Run and compare the values with their positions.

00:00:30.232 --> 00:00:34.722
This distinction is useful. Sometimes we only need the highest value.

00:00:34.722 --> 00:00:39.467
Other times we need to know which observation produced it.

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:44.597
For example, if each position corresponds to a store, product, day, or model,

00:00:44.597 --> 00:00:50.947
argmax lets us identify the winning position and then connect that position to other information.

00:00:50.947 --> 00:00:56.427
Remember that argmax returns an index, not the actual maximum value.

00:00:56.427 --> 00:00:59.760
That small distinction prevents many beginner mistakes.
